# Rebuilding px4-userland @VERSION@

This corresponding-source archive records repository commit `@COMMIT@` and
tree `@TREE@`. The `repository/` directory is the exact tracked source tree;
`third_party/libusb-1.0.30/` and its original verified source archive are the
libusb sources used for the static Linux, macOS, and Android binaries.

## Linux static build and IFD variants

Build the production executables in Alpine/musl, then build the matching PC/SC
IFD in a host-libc environment. The glibc IFD must be built in Debian 11 or an
equivalent glibc 2.31 baseline; the musl IFD must be built in the matching
Alpine environment:

```sh
scripts/build-linux-static.sh --output build-linux-static \
  --libusb-source-archive third_party/libusb-1.0.30.tar.bz2
scripts/build-linux-ifd.sh --libc glibc --output build-linux-ifd-glibc
scripts/build-linux-ifd.sh --libc musl --output build-linux-ifd-musl
scripts/test-static-relink.sh \
  --libusb-source-archive third_party/libusb-1.0.30.tar.bz2
```

Package each libc-qualified archive with the same static executable directory:

```sh
version=$(tr -d '\n' < VERSION)
scripts/package-artifact.py --platform linux-glibc-x86_64 --version "$version" \
  --static-build-dir build-linux-static --ifd-library build-linux-ifd-glibc/px4-userland-ifd.so \
  --reader-template packaging/pcsc/reader.conf.d/px4-userland.conf.in \
  --source-ref SOURCE_COMMIT --output-dir dist
scripts/package-artifact.py --platform linux-musl-x86_64 --version "$version" \
  --static-build-dir build-linux-static --ifd-library build-linux-ifd-musl/px4-userland-ifd.so \
  --reader-template packaging/pcsc/reader.conf.d/px4-userland.conf.in \
  --source-ref SOURCE_COMMIT --output-dir dist
```

The aarch64 commands are identical on a native aarch64 build host. The four
archive names are libc-qualified; a generic Linux archive is not produced.

## Android rebuild and LGPL relink

Install Android NDK r27, CMake, Ninja, a POSIX shell, Python 3, Autoconf build
tools, and set `ANDROID_NDK_HOME` to the NDK root. From this archive root:

```sh
cd repository
scripts/build-android.sh \
  --abi arm64-v8a \
  --libusb-source ../third_party/libusb-1.0.30 \
  --output ../rebuilt-android-aarch64
scripts/build-android.sh \
  --abi armeabi-v7a \
  --libusb-source ../third_party/libusb-1.0.30 \
  --output ../rebuilt-android-armv7a
scripts/build-android.sh \
  --abi x86_64 \
  --libusb-source ../third_party/libusb-1.0.30 \
  --output ../rebuilt-android-x86_64
```

The Android archive also contains the architecture-independent `px4-termux`
launcher. It uses the Termux-provided shell and nested `termux-usb` calls to
pass two explicitly selected USB device FDs to `px4d`; it is not linked with
libusb and is not part of the ELF static-link inventory.

To relink with a modified LGPL libusb, modify a copy of
`third_party/libusb-1.0.30/` and pass that directory to `--libusb-source`.
The production release evidence path intentionally accepts only the pinned,
checksum-verified libusb source archive; local relink builds do not emit that
release evidence.

## macOS arm64 rebuild and LGPL relink

Install the Xcode command line tools, CMake, Ninja, and Homebrew pcsc-lite
(for the IFD headers only). From this archive root, build libusb 1.0.30 as a
static library from the verified source archive, then `px4d` linked against
it together with `px4-ts`, `px4ctl`, and the IFD bundle:

```sh
cd repository
scripts/build-macos-static.sh --build-dir ../build-macos \
  --pcsc-include-dir "$(brew --prefix pcsc-lite)/include/PCSC" \
  --libusb-source-archive ../third_party/libusb-1.0.30.tar.bz2
scripts/test-static-relink.sh \
  --libusb-source-archive ../third_party/libusb-1.0.30.tar.bz2
```

To relink with a modified LGPL libusb, modify a copy of
`third_party/libusb-1.0.30/` and pass that directory to
`scripts/build-macos-static.sh --libusb-source-dir` instead of
`--libusb-source-archive`. The script links libusb's `Libs.private` system
frameworks (IOKit, CoreFoundation, Security) and `libobjc`. The IFD bundle
does not link libusb. Firmware is neither required to compile nor present in
this archive.

## Windows x64 rebuild and LGPL DLL replacement

Install CMake, Ninja (or samurai/samu), Make, a POSIX shell, Python 3, curl, `tar`, `xz`, and `sha256sum`.
All commands below run from this archive root (the directory containing `repository/` and `third_party/`).

`scripts/build-windows.sh` verifies and extracts the pinned toolchain and libusb source archives into a private
temporary work directory that it removes on exit. Its `--cache` directory holds only the downloaded archives,
not an extracted toolchain tree. Preseed the bundled, already-verified libusb archive so the production rebuild
uses the corresponding source instead of downloading it, then cross-build the Phase 1 executables:

```sh
mkdir -p toolchain-cache
cp third_party/libusb-1.0.30.tar.bz2 toolchain-cache/
repository/scripts/build-windows.sh --output build-windows --cache "$PWD/toolchain-cache"
```

The toolchain and libusb versions and their SHA-256 values are fixed in the script. The archive ships the exact
narrow llvm-mingw runtime license texts under `toolchain/`; no compiler binary or toolchain source bulk is
included.

`px4d.exe` dynamically loads `libusb-1.0.dll`, which remains LGPL-2.1-or-later. To replace the DLL with one
built from a modified libusb source, verify the pinned toolchain archive, extract it into a fresh owned
directory inside this archive root, and use the absolute compiler path from there:

```sh
echo 'f83556c9ffa4d4291fadea1a0776c1383332dacdf4d7fbdf974c2928cb32c6f7  toolchain-cache/llvm-mingw-20250910-ucrt-ubuntu-22.04-x86_64.tar.xz' | sha256sum -c -
mkdir toolchain
tar -xf toolchain-cache/llvm-mingw-20250910-ucrt-ubuntu-22.04-x86_64.tar.xz -C toolchain
toolchain="$PWD/toolchain/llvm-mingw-20250910-ucrt-ubuntu-22.04-x86_64"

# Modify a copy of the bundled source, then build the shared DLL with the same flags the build script uses.
cp -R third_party/libusb-1.0.30 build-libusb
cd build-libusb
./configure --host=x86_64-w64-mingw32 --prefix="$PWD/../build-libusb-prefix" \
  --enable-shared --disable-static --disable-udev \
  --disable-examples-build --disable-tests-build \
  CC="$toolchain/bin/x86_64-w64-mingw32-clang" \
  AR="$toolchain/bin/llvm-ar" RANLIB="$toolchain/bin/llvm-ranlib" \
  CFLAGS="-O2 -g0 -ffile-prefix-map=$PWD=. -fdebug-prefix-map=$PWD=. -fmacro-prefix-map=$PWD=." \
  LDFLAGS="-Wl,-s -Wl,--no-insert-timestamp -Wl,--build-id=none"
make
make install
```

Replace `build-windows/libusb-1.0.dll` (or the same file inside an extracted Windows archive) with
`build-libusb-prefix/bin/libusb-1.0.dll`, keeping the same file name and the libusb-1.0 ABI and export set.
The production release path accepts only the pinned, checksum-verified libusb source archive; local relink
builds do not emit release evidence. Firmware is neither required nor present in this archive.
